WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.467
-You look fantastic.
-Thank you.

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:03.801
-Welcome back to the show.
Thanks for coming on.

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:05.834
-It's so great to be here.
-I always love seeing you.

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:07.934
You spend a lot of time here
in New York.

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:09.367
-I did.
-Do you feel good when you come

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:11.067
back and you see the city
opening up?

00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:13.767
-I love this city.
I went to school --

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:15.434
I went to NYU for grad school.

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:17.167
It's where I sort of
became an actor.

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:19.501
-Yeah. NYU is not an easy school
to get into.

00:00:19.501 --> 00:00:20.868
-No, it's not.

00:00:20.868 --> 00:00:24.400
-Did you know that you were
getting in?

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.534
-Okay.
So, I came for a callback.

00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:30.100
The program has about 800 people
try out for the MFA program.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.367
They take 50 people
for a callback and then

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:34.734
18 people are allowed in.
-Wow.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.834
-So, my first time coming in
was for my callback to NYU.

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:39.634
My friend lived at Astor Place.

00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:42.367
1 Astor Place, which is
right across the street

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:44.167
from 721 Broadway.

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:46.167
So that's where I lived
for the three years.

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:49.400
I could wake up at 8:55,
make it to class by 9:00.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.300
I'm blessed, bro.
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.968
-Oh, yeah, yeah.
-My whole life, it's like,

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:54.667
"You five minutes away
from school, Brown?"

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:56.968
I was like, "Yeah, man. I'm five
minutes away from school."

00:00:56.968 --> 00:01:00.200
-Yeah, the life is pretty good.
But Astor Place is gorgeous.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.601
-Astor Place is awesome.
I remember this too, Jimmy.

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:06.234
I remember seeing you in front
of Cozy Soup &amp; Burger.

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:09.467
This is crazy. This is before
Jimmy had a side part.

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:11.000
Like, this was like --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.234
This is Jimmy, like,
low-level Jimmy.

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:20.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:22.701
This was back in the day.

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:26.534
Jimmy would have his guitar
and was just sitting down.

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:28.968
And he'd be strumming along,
just doing his thing.

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:30.334
I'm, like, "Hey, man,
you're really good."

00:01:30.334 --> 00:01:32.267
"Aw, thanks buddy.
Thanks, I appreciate that."

00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:34.200
[ Laughter ]
-That's a good impression.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.267
-Thank you very much.
I appreciate it.

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:36.267
-Wait, I was playing in front of
a Cozy?

00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:38.701
-Yeah, dude.
-I love Cozy sandwiches.

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:39.734
-See, that's what I'm saying.

00:01:39.734 --> 00:01:41.868
No, no, it was
Cozy Soup &amp; burger.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:44.367
You were on Broadway
just chilling.

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:45.567
I don't even know
if you were like --

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:47.534
You may have still been
on "SNL."

00:01:47.534 --> 00:01:49.534
But you were just like
jamming on the guitar,

00:01:49.534 --> 00:01:51.667
hanging out,
playing for the people.

00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:53.434
-Yeah.
-That's who Jimmy Fallon is.

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:54.767
[ Cheers and applause ]
He's one of the people.

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:56.467
-That was fun.
I love that you saw that.

00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:58.234
No way!
-Yes!

00:01:58.234 --> 00:02:02.000
-That's crazy. What -- Did
you -- What other sightings?

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.801
Who else did you meet?
-I see a lot of people.

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:05.267
So, that's the thing about
New York City.

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:07.567
You get a chance to see
celebrities all the time.

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:10.400
And everybody's very cool.
You just kind of go up to people

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:11.701
and like,
"Hey, man, love your work."

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:13.067
They're like,
"Hey, man, thanks a lot."

00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:15.267
You see Buscemi, Billy Crudup.

00:02:15.267 --> 00:02:17.601
Sam Shepard I remember running
into in the audience.

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:20.734
And it's interesting too because
now having a little taste

00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:23.033
of fame myself,
it's really cool.

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:24.300
You never get tired of people
saying,

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.567
"Hey, man, I love your work."
-Isn't that great?

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:26.901
-And you're like, "Thanks, man.
Appreciate it."

00:02:26.901 --> 00:02:28.601
You know what I'm saying?
They like, "Are you Sterling?

00:02:28.601 --> 00:02:30.000
Hey, man, I love your work."
It's cool.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.567
-Yeah. And you think back to
when you were saying that --

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:33.868
-And I think back to when I was
saying that to other people.

00:02:33.868 --> 00:02:36.934
So, it's like it's a perfect
sort of like --

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:38.634
They're not stopping your day.

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:40.267
You keep moving and everything
like that.

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:42.234
And then every once in a while,
you meet somebody that's like,

00:02:42.234 --> 00:02:46.234
just uber enthusiasm and you
recognize it as uber enthusiasm.

00:02:46.234 --> 00:02:48.934
But it's a little strange too
because it's like, "It's you."

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:51.334
[ Laughter ]
And I'm like, "Yeah, it's me."

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:53.200
And they're like, "Oh, my God,
it's really you!"

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:56.834
And so everything stops
for a moment.

00:02:56.834 --> 00:03:00.400
But I remember that feeling of
meeting somebody

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.567
whose work you loved, and you
can't give people the gas face.

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:06.267
Like, that's the worst thing
when people just walk past you

00:03:06.267 --> 00:03:07.567
like they didn't even see you.

00:03:07.567 --> 00:03:10.267
So I vowed I will never give
anybody the gas face.

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:12.033
I may have to go,
like, get to my kids.

00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:14.300
And I'll tell you, "I got
a kid that needs me.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:17.400
I love you too." But I never
give anybody the gas face.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.834
-You got to give everyone
time of day.

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:20.534
-Absolutely.
-You say thanks so much.

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:22.667
Is there any celeb that you have
not met yet

00:03:22.667 --> 00:03:24.834
where you were like,
"I would freak out."

00:03:24.834 --> 00:03:26.567
"Hello, hi."

00:03:26.567 --> 00:03:30.133
-I've been in the presence of
Streep three times.

00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:31.601
-Streep.
-She don't need a first name.

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:32.734
You know who I'm talking about.

00:03:32.734 --> 00:03:35.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:35.934 --> 00:03:39.033
Jimmy, I've been in Streep's
presence three times.

00:03:39.033 --> 00:03:40.634
One time I was working
at the Public.

00:03:40.634 --> 00:03:42.200
And she was doing something else
at the Public.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:43.434
And she was just talking to
people.

00:03:43.434 --> 00:03:45.934
And I was just standing.
Camera, follow me, please.

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:47.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:49.267
I was just standing there
like...

00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:52.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.801 --> 00:03:54.067
"It's Streep, y'all."

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:56.133
And she was just talking,
being regular old Streep.

00:03:56.133 --> 00:03:58.234
And I'm like, "No, I can't --
I don't know --"

00:03:58.234 --> 00:04:01.767
I didn't -- I couldn't talk.
-You just lurked?

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:04.767
-I just lurked. I was weird.
I was a creeper.

00:04:04.767 --> 00:04:06.667
-You were a creeper.
-So, I'm looking forward to

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:08.033
somebody who knows both of us

00:04:08.033 --> 00:04:09.801
to hopefully give me
an introduction.

00:04:09.801 --> 00:04:11.167
-I think you two
will hit it off.

00:04:11.167 --> 00:04:13.567
-Yeah. I think so. You know her.
You know everybody.

00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:15.968
-No, no, no. I still freak out
though when I see Streep.

00:04:15.968 --> 00:04:19.534
-Who do you -- do you fr-- You
get a chance to meet everybody.

00:04:19.534 --> 00:04:22.467
Who do you geek over?
Is it more musicians?

00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:24.067
Is it more athletes?
Is it actors?

00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:26.300
Like, politicians?
Like, who do you geek?

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:29.801
-I geek too much. I'm a super
fan over too many people.

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:31.300
I need to calm down.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.734
I freak out -- I freaked out
when I saw you in the hallway.

00:04:33.734 --> 00:04:35.133
-Stop it.

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:38.434
-I jumped up, wrapped my legs
around you.

00:04:38.434 --> 00:04:40.400
You're like, "Get off. Dude,
I'll see you in five minutes!"

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.534
-We do both have side parts now,

00:04:42.534 --> 00:04:44.434
which was something that we
talked about backstage.

00:04:44.434 --> 00:04:46.000
-Yeah, yeah.
-This wasn't 10 years ago.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.000
-No, look at us.
We've grown, we've grown.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.567
-This is us now.
-Can we talk about your new

00:04:49.567 --> 00:04:52.033
movie, "Honk for Jesus.
Save Your Soul"?

00:04:52.033 --> 00:04:56.133
-I would love to.
-You play a pastor.

00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:58.300
I've had people on the show.
We talked about -- Some people

00:04:58.300 --> 00:04:59.701
say like, oh, maybe
they may have gotten

00:04:59.701 --> 00:05:01.934
their start in church.
-Sure.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:05.567
-Or going on the altar or going
to church or performing.

00:05:05.567 --> 00:05:08.234
Did you feel that way?
-I love church.

00:05:08.234 --> 00:05:10.033
I am a deep man of faith.

00:05:10.033 --> 00:05:12.667
And so it's a deep part of
who I am as a person.

00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:16.434
My best friend, Philip Grant --
if he sees this, I get to shout

00:05:16.434 --> 00:05:18.033
his name out on national TV.

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:20.300
His mom and dad
had their own church.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.067
So, he's a P.K.
And it was a basement turned --

00:05:22.067 --> 00:05:24.000
-He's a P.K.?
-Preacher's kid. Sorry.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.501
Preacher's kid. P.K.
Some of you know that.

00:05:26.501 --> 00:05:30.767
Okay. His parents ran church out
of the bottom of their --

00:05:30.767 --> 00:05:32.734
the basement of their house.
And I would go over to his house

00:05:32.734 --> 00:05:34.601
because he lived right around
the corner from me.

00:05:34.601 --> 00:05:36.968
And they would ask me to
summarize like the Bible study.

00:05:36.968 --> 00:05:38.767
And I'd get up -- you know,
I've always had a little bit

00:05:38.767 --> 00:05:40.834
of the gift of the gab
and I love, you know,

00:05:40.834 --> 00:05:42.467
summarizing things
and seeming smart.

00:05:42.467 --> 00:05:44.467
That was the other thing.
I loved when his parents would

00:05:44.467 --> 00:05:46.267
be like, "Why don't you be more
like Kelby?"

00:05:46.267 --> 00:05:49.033
Sterling K. Brown, Kelby.
Went by Kelby.

00:05:49.033 --> 00:05:50.667
"Why don't you be more like
Kelby, Phil?

00:05:50.667 --> 00:05:53.434
He's so smart and so articulate
and everything."

00:05:53.434 --> 00:05:56.033
And Philip would just be like,
"This Negro." Anyway --

00:05:56.033 --> 00:05:57.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:59.667
-He's like,
"This guy. This guy."

00:05:59.667 --> 00:06:01.601
-"This guy." That's what I
should've said. "This guy."

00:06:01.601 --> 00:06:03.367
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.367 --> 00:06:05.067
-You know what I'm saying?
-I know what you're saying.

00:06:05.067 --> 00:06:07.033
-You know what I'm saying.

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:10.467
So, I would do it, and I would
summarize the Bible study.

00:06:10.467 --> 00:06:13.000
And they'd say, "Ooh, Kelby
gonna be a preacher."

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.067
And Kelby would be like,
"No, I'm not."

00:06:15.067 --> 00:06:18.868
But I did know that there was
something about speaking

00:06:18.868 --> 00:06:22.367
in front of people, the
performative aspects of, like,

00:06:22.367 --> 00:06:23.868
being in front of a crowd
or whatnot.

00:06:23.868 --> 00:06:26.501
I was like, "Maybe I'll parlay
this into something different."

00:06:26.501 --> 00:06:27.934
And now, here we are.
-Yeah.

00:06:27.934 --> 00:06:29.901
And you've done a fantastic --

00:06:29.901 --> 00:06:31.934
You can move people
with your performance.

00:06:31.934 --> 00:06:33.200
-Thanks.
-And that's what you do.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:37.501
And in this -- I love that
this film got made.

00:06:37.501 --> 00:06:40.334
And all of a sudden,
Jordan Peele heard about this

00:06:40.334 --> 00:06:41.634
and was like, "Oh, I want to
produce this."

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:44.367
And Daniel Kaluuya.
-Yeah, they're awesome people.

00:06:44.367 --> 00:06:46.834
Big up to "Nope." Great movie.

00:06:46.834 --> 00:06:48.000
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.167
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Absolutely.

00:06:49.167 --> 00:06:51.234
-Keke!
-Keke.

00:06:51.234 --> 00:06:52.367
Lord have mercy.
-Keke Palmer.

00:06:52.367 --> 00:06:53.934
-That girl. Lord have mercy.

00:06:53.934 --> 00:06:55.534
-Watch out, watch out.

00:06:55.534 --> 00:06:58.601
-Daniel and I got a chance to do
"Black Panther" together.

00:06:58.601 --> 00:07:00.434
Met him during that time.
-That's right.

00:07:00.434 --> 00:07:03.067
-And so, he's a producer on
this film along with Jordan.

00:07:03.067 --> 00:07:04.534
And he'll call up every once
in a while.

00:07:04.534 --> 00:07:05.601
"What's up, bruv,
how you doing?"

00:07:05.601 --> 00:07:06.834
I'm like, "I'm great, man."

00:07:06.834 --> 00:07:08.734
He's like, "Yeah, we in London
right now, man.

00:07:08.734 --> 00:07:10.501
Can't wait to get back over
there for the premiere.

00:07:10.501 --> 00:07:12.868
It's going to be fantastic."

00:07:12.868 --> 00:07:14.234
-That's a good Daniel Kaluuya,
yeah.

00:07:14.234 --> 00:07:15.467
-Thank you, man.
I appreciate it.

00:07:15.467 --> 00:07:18.267
What I love about being an actor
right now --

00:07:18.267 --> 00:07:19.934
being a Black actor is that,

00:07:19.934 --> 00:07:22.133
there's a lot of folks doing
a lot of different things.

00:07:22.133 --> 00:07:24.767
And there's more than enough
for everybody to eat.

00:07:24.767 --> 00:07:26.434
Everybody's got a seat
at the table.

00:07:26.434 --> 00:07:28.834
So there's no sort of sense
that if I get something,

00:07:28.834 --> 00:07:30.400
I'm taking it away from
somebody else

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:32.868
or if Daniel gets something,
Brian Henry --

00:07:32.868 --> 00:07:34.000
anybody gets something else.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.834
Like, everybody feels
comfortable.

00:07:35.834 --> 00:07:37.801
And we get a chance to celebrate
each other.

00:07:37.801 --> 00:07:39.167
And that's a beautiful place
to be.

00:07:39.167 --> 00:07:40.801
-That's great.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:40.801 --> 00:07:44.300
I agree.

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:47.167
The movie is --
The movie's really funny.

00:07:47.167 --> 00:07:49.000
-Thank you, man.
-It's really funny.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.634
"Honk for Jesus. Save Your Soul"
is the title.

00:07:51.634 --> 00:07:54.567
So, yeah, how do we set it up?

00:07:54.567 --> 00:07:55.801
Basically, the church --

00:07:55.801 --> 00:07:58.200
-Basically, before the movie
begins,

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.334
there's a scandal that happened
to these two --

00:08:00.334 --> 00:08:02.968
to the pastor and first lady of
this mega church.

00:08:02.968 --> 00:08:05.133
Wander to Greater Paths
Baptist Church.

00:08:05.133 --> 00:08:08.734
Pastor Lee-Curtis Childs and my
partner in crime, Regina Hall,

00:08:08.734 --> 00:08:11.667
who plays Trinitie Childs,
who is amazing.

00:08:11.667 --> 00:08:12.667
-She is amazing.

00:08:12.667 --> 00:08:13.968
-There's a scandal.

00:08:13.968 --> 00:08:15.767
They lose their congregation.

00:08:15.767 --> 00:08:18.501
They hire a documentary film
crew to sort of chart

00:08:18.501 --> 00:08:20.200
their ascendence
back to prominence

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:21.834
as they get their congregation
back.

00:08:21.834 --> 00:08:22.968
So, that's what it's about.

00:08:22.968 --> 00:08:24.434
-Getting their congregation
back.

00:08:24.434 --> 00:08:26.667
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's Sterling K. Brown in

00:08:26.667 --> 00:08:28.400
"Honk for Jesus.
Save Your Soul."

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.801
Take a look at this.

00:08:29.801 --> 00:08:32.167
-Now, I'm telling y'all, you
should have seen this place

00:08:32.167 --> 00:08:33.467
when it was jumping.

00:08:33.467 --> 00:08:35.200
-Of course, it hasn't looked
like that for a while.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:36.300
-No.
-Obviously.

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:37.834
-No.
-But we're going to get

00:08:37.834 --> 00:08:39.801
that all back.
-Oh, yeah, we will.

00:08:39.801 --> 00:08:42.868
-Have this place looking all --
Oh [bleep]

00:08:42.868 --> 00:08:45.000
-Oh, oh, boy.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.734
-[Bleep]
-Oh, my goodness.

00:08:46.734 --> 00:08:48.534
-Now, how in the good Lord's
lush green Earth

00:08:48.534 --> 00:08:49.834
is anybody supposed to take me

00:08:49.834 --> 00:08:51.667
and the resurrection of
my church seriously?

00:08:51.667 --> 00:08:53.534
These are Fianos.
-Yes.

00:08:53.534 --> 00:08:56.400
-Those are --
That's an Italian brand.

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:00.234
-We can edit around that.
Right, Anita?

00:09:00.234 --> 00:09:02.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:04.334
-Italian brand.
-Italian brand.

00:09:04.334 --> 00:09:06.434
Just in case.

